169:\label{eq:interpolant}
174:**Proven.** The first exact obstruction to a real degree-N comparator is \(K=\lfloor(N+1)/2\rfloor+1\). Three positive carriers exclude N up to four, but a fifth-degree real comparator interpolates them. With complex coefficients and only positive-frequency samples, interpolation permits K up to N+1 and the first obstruction occurs at N+2. No finite polynomial equals a nonzero single-pole response on an open frequency interval.
